#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_marketplace_base
msgid ""
"The product name shown on the website, in search and in orders. Write the "
"Arabic name, then the English one with the language button next to the "
"field."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The subcategory of the product (for example Generators, Loaders, Filters). "
"It decides the section of the website, the fields shown below, the filters "
"and the link of the product. Inside a section only that section's "
"subcategories are offered. Required."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The maker of the product, chosen from the brand list (Marketplace > "
"Configuration > Brands). A main filter on the website and part of the "
"search. Required."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The model or family of the machine (for example P110-5), from the list of "
"its brand's models. Used in search, and it links the spare parts that fit "
"this machine. Required for equipment."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The equipment models this part fits, one or more. It powers the 'choose your"
" machine' filter and the parts suggested with each machine. Required for "
"spare parts."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"Other names people use for this product, separated by commas, in Arabic or "
"English (for example: diesel genset, مولد ديزل). Search on the website also "
"looks here. Optional, not shown to the customer."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"Tags that describe the product (family, type, size such as 'oil filters', "
"'15W-40'). Used for filtering and search, and new tags can be added. "
"Required for spare parts."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"Where the product comes from: Original, China or Egypt. A filter on the "
"website. Required."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"New, used or refurbished. A used or refurbished machine also needs the year,"
" the operating hours, the operation video and the meter and data plate "
"photos, and may need an inspection before it is published. Oils and filters "
"are new only. Required."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The capacity or power of the machine as a number, read with the unit next to"
" it (for example 250 kVA, 3 ton). The most important filter in every "
"equipment category. Required for equipment."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The unit of the capacity: kVA, kW, ton, cubic metre, ampere, metre or litre."
" Shown with the capacity."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"What powers the machine: diesel, petrol, gas, electric or hybrid. A filter "
"on the website."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The maker's number of the part, exactly as written on it. The first thing a "
"technician searches for. Required for spare parts."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The numbers of the same part at other makers, separated by commas (for "
"example LF3349, P550162). Search finds the part by any of them. Optional, "
"not shown to the customer."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The sources the customer may order this part in (Original, China, Egypt). "
"Empty: only the single source above."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The size or volume of the part when it matters, for example the litres of an"
" oil pack. Shown in the specifications. Optional."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid "The unit of the size or volume (litre, metre...)."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The price the customer pays, in the company currency. Empty or zero: the "
"product shows 'request a quote' instead of a price. A price-range filter on "
"the website."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"Whether the machine is offered for sale or for rent. For rent shows the "
"rental path on the website and needs the rent per day."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The vendor's rent price for one day. The website shows it with the "
"platform's rent margin added. Required when the machine is for rent."
msgstr ""

#. module: leaders_marketplace
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:leaders_marketplace.view_product_template_leaders_catalog
msgid ""
"The quantity on hand in the warehouses, for information only. Stock is "
"updated from Inventory or by the vendor in their portal."
